# Papervine rules

## Before you start

Read the project's `docs.json` first. It defines the site's navigation, theme, colors, and
configuration. Papervine never infers structure from folder layout — the sidebar is exactly
what `docs.json` says it is.

Search for existing content before creating a page. Updating a page, adding a section, or
linking to what exists usually beats writing a new page.

Read 2-3 similar pages first to match the site's voice, structure, and formatting.

## File conventions

- The config file is `docs.json`, at the root of the docs folder.
- Pages are `.mdx` (`.md` also renders). Match the directory's existing naming; default to
  kebab-case (`getting-started.mdx`).
- A page missing from `docs.json` navigation still renders at its URL but appears in no
  sidebar. Add it to a group unless you deliberately want it unlisted.
- Nav entries are paths relative to the docs root **without the extension**:
  `"guides/auth"` means `guides/auth.mdx`. The index page is written `"index"`.

### Internal links

- Use root-relative paths with no file extension: `/getting-started/quickstart`.
- Never use relative paths (`../page`) or absolute URLs for internal pages — a site can be
  served from a subdomain, a custom domain, or a path prefix, and only root-relative links
  survive all three.

### Images

Keep images in the repository and reference them root-relative. Every image needs
descriptive alt text.

```mdx
![The deploy log after a successful sync](/images/deploy-log.png)
```

## Page frontmatter

Set `title` and `description` on every page. `description` is the line search results and
social previews show, so write a real one.

```yaml
---
title: "Connect a repository"
description: "Point Papervine at a Git repo of MDX and docs.json, and publish on push."
---
```

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| `title` | string | Recommended | Page `<h1>`, sidebar label, and browser title. Derived from the slug if omitted. |
| `description` | string | Recommended | Summary under the heading; used by search, `llms.txt`, and social cards. |
| `sidebarTitle` | string | No | Shorter label for the sidebar when the title is long. |
| `icon` | string | No | Lucide icon name shown beside the sidebar entry. |
| `tag` | string | No | Small badge next to the sidebar entry (e.g. `NEW`). |
| `hidden` | boolean | No | Omit from the sidebar; still reachable by URL. |
| `noindex` | boolean | No | Exclude from search, `llms.txt`, and search engines. |
| `keywords` | string[] | No | Extra search terms. |
| `url` | string | No | Sidebar entry links here instead of to the page. |
| `groups` | string[] | No | Restrict the page to those reader-auth groups. |
| `public` | boolean | No | Opt a page out of group gating. |

Any key containing a colon (`og:image`, `twitter:card`) is emitted as a `<meta>` tag and
overrides the site-wide `seo.metatags` value.

Unknown frontmatter keys are ignored rather than treated as errors.

## Writing standards

- **Second person, present tense.** "You connect a repo", not "the user connects a repo".
- **Say what it does before how to configure it.** A reader who lands mid-page from search
  needs the sentence that orients them.
- **Sentence case in headings and code-block titles.** Title Case reads as branding.
- **Every fence gets a language.** It is what produces highlighting, and an untagged block is
  rendered as plain grey text.
- **Every image gets alt text describing what it shows**, not what it is — "the dashboard after
  a first sync" beats "screenshot".
- **A `description` on every page.** It is the line search results, `llms.txt` and social cards
  use, so a missing one costs a reader the choice of whether to open the page.
- **No emoji, no filler, no superlatives.** "Simply", "just", "powerful" and "seamless" all
  survive deletion.
- **Prefer a shorter page to a longer one.** Two pages with real titles beat one with four
  levels of heading.
- **Don't repeat the `title` as an `# H1`.** The title already renders as the page heading, so
  a second one gives the page two competing headings and a confusing outline.

## Common mistakes

- Relative links (`../page`) instead of root-relative (`/section/page`).
- File extensions in internal links (`/page.mdx` instead of `/page`).
- Forgetting to add a new page to `docs.json` navigation.
- A code block with no language tag (use ` ```python `, not ` ``` `).
- Images without alt text.
- `"hidden": true` on a **tab** — it is ignored. Mark the tab's groups instead; a tab with no
  reachable pages disappears on its own.
- A Font Awesome or Tabler icon name. Papervine resolves **Lucide** names only; an unknown
  name renders nothing. Use `<Icon src="/path.svg" />` for anything else.
- A trailing comma in `docs.json`. It is strict JSON, and an unparseable config is the usual
  cause of a site that renders but looks unstyled.
